From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Synkar <dev@synkar.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 19:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] rockchip: rkvenc: fix imported dma-buf size for multi-seg buffers

rkvenc_dma_import_fd() derives the imported buffer size from the first
scatterlist entry only (sg_dma_len(sgt->sgl)). That is only valid when
the dma-buf is physically contiguous (single sg entry), which is the
case for CMA-backed buffers.

The Rockchip MPP userspace on a mainline kernel allocates encoder input
buffers through the dma-buf heaps allocator (/dev/dma_heap). With
CONFIG_DMABUF_HEAPS_SYSTEM (system heap), allocations are page-scattered
and the returned sg table has multiple entries. In that case the driver
reports a too-small buffer size, and the task guardrail rejects any
register whose intra-buffer offset exceeds the (underreported) first
segment length, e.g. the UV plane of a 1080p NV12 frame (offset
1920*1080) in a 1 MiB first segment.

Sum the dma lengths over the whole sg table so ->size reflects the full
buffer.

Signed-off-by: Synkar <dev@synkar.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvenc/rkvenc_iommu.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvenc/rkvenc_iommu.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvenc/rkvenc_iommu.c
@@ -183,8 +183,15 @@ rkvenc_dma_import_fd(struct rkvenc_iommu_info *iommu_info,
 		rkvenc_err("dma_buf_map_attachment fd %d failed(%d)\n", fd, ret);
 		goto fail_map;
 	}
 	buffer->iova = sg_dma_address(sgt->sgl);
-	buffer->size = sg_dma_len(sgt->sgl);
+	{
+		struct scatterlist *sg;
+		size_t size = 0;
+
+		for (sg = sgt->sgl; sg; sg = sg_next(sg))
+			size += sg_dma_len(sg);
+		buffer->size = size;
+	}
 	buffer->attach = attach;
 	buffer->sgt = sgt;
 	buffer->dma = dma;
